3-4a9b-931f-e70e45217b42.png" alt=3D""></strong></span></span></li></ol><p>=
&nbsp;</p></details><details open=3D""><summary><a id=3D"B4"><span style=3D=
"color:#000000;"><span><strong>How to update BIOS in the MyASUS in UEFI mod=
e</strong></span></span></a></summary><p>In the MyASUS in UEFI interface, y=
ou can navigate and confirm using the <strong>Arrow Keys and Enter key on t=
he keyboard</strong>, <strong>Touchpad</strong>, or <strong>Mouse</strong>.=
</p><p><strong>Note</strong>: The BIOS update screen below may vary slightl=
y depending on the model.</p><ol><li>After entering the BIOS Utility, go to=
 the <strong>Advanced Settings</strong> by pressing <strong>Hotkey[F7]</str=
ong> or use <strong>cursor </strong>to click<span style=3D"color:#FF0000;">=
<span>=E2=91=A0</span></span>.&nbsp;<br><img class=3D"image_resized" style=
=3D"width:800px;" src=3D"https://km-ap.asus.com/uploads/PhotoLibrarys/8a53f=
c79-6a00-4a96-8408-a7e886967aef/20240318143314383_EN_1.png"></li><li>After =
entering the Advanced Settings, select <strong>[Advanced]</strong> screen<s=
pan style=3D"color:#FF0000;"><span>=E2=91=A1</span></span>, and then select=
 <strong>[ASUS Firmware Update]</strong> item<span style=3D"color:#FF0000;"=
><span>=E2=91=A2</span></span>.&nbsp;<br><img class=3D"image_resized" style=
=3D"width:800px;" src=3D"https://km-ap.asus.com/uploads/PhotoLibrarys/8a53f=
c79-6a00-4a96-8408-a7e886967aef/20240318143314326_EN_2.png"></li><li>Select=
 the <strong>storage device where the BIOS file located</strong><span style=
=3D"color:#FF0000;"><span>=E2=91=A3</span></span>, then click the <strong>B=
IOS file</strong><span style=3D"color:#FF0000;"><span>=E2=91=A4</span></spa=
n>.&nbsp;<br>The BIOS file naming convention for ASUS devices follows the f=
ormat of <strong>'Model'</strong>AS.<strong>'BIOS Version'</strong>, as ill=
ustrated by the example X1505ZAAS.310, where the model is X1505ZA and the B=
IOS version is 310.&nbsp;<br><span style=3D"color:#FF0000;"><span><strong>N=
ote: Ensure that the device maintains a battery level of 20% or higher and =
is connected to a power source before proceeding with the BIOS update.</str=
ong></span></span>&nbsp;<br><img class=3D"image_resized" style=3D"width:800=
px;" src=3D"https://km-ap.asus.com/uploads/PhotoLibrarys/8a53fc79-6a00-4a96=
-8408-a7e886967aef/20240318143314309_EN_3.png"></li><li>When prompted to co=
nfirm whether you wish to proceed with the update, please click on <strong>=
[Confirm]</strong><span style=3D"color:#FF0000;"><span>=E2=91=A5</span></sp=
an>.&nbsp;<br><img class=3D"image_resized" style=3D"width:800px;" src=3D"ht=
tps://km-ap.asus.com/uploads/PhotoLibrarys/8a53fc79-6a00-4a96-8408-a7e88696=
7aef/20240318143314380_EN_4.png"></li><li>Verify whether the BIOS file info=
rmation for updating is correct, then click on <strong>[Confirm]</strong><s=
pan style=3D"color:#FF0000;"><span>=E2=91=A6</span></span>.&nbsp;<br><img c=
lass=3D"image_resized" style=3D"width:800px;" src=3D"https://km-ap.asus.com=
/uploads/PhotoLibrarys/8a53fc79-6a00-4a96-8408-a7e886967aef/202403181433143=
07_EN_5.png"></li><li>The device is currently performing a BIOS update. Ple=
ase wait patiently for the BIOS update to complete. Once the update is fini=
shed, the device will automatically restart and boot into the Windows opera=
ting system.&nbsp;<br><span style=3D"color:#FF0000;"><span><strong>Note: En=
sure that the device is connected to power and do not force shutdown during=
 the BIOS update to prevent any abnormal issues.</strong></span></span>&nbs=
p;<br><img class=3D"image_resized" style=3D"width:800px;" src=3D"https://km=
-ap.asus.com/uploads/PhotoLibrarys/8a53fc79-6a00-4a96-8408-a7e886967aef/202=
